  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Consider the equation $\\dfrac{\\sin2x+\\sin x}{\\cos2x+\\cos x+1}=\\sqrt3$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-4-slot-4-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\dfrac{\\sin2x+\\sin x}{\\cos2x+\\cos x+1}=\\tan x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sin2x+\\sin x}{\\cos2x+\\cos x+1}=\\tan x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin2x+\\sin x}{\\cos2x+\\cos x+1}&=\\frac{2\\sin x\\cos x+\\sin x}{2\\cos^2x-1+\\cos x+1}\\\\&=\\frac{\\sin x(2\\cos x+1)}{2\\cos^2x+\\cos x}\\\\&=\\frac{\\sin x(2\\cos x+1)}{\\cos x(2\\cos x+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\\\&=\\tan x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-4-slot-4-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence solve the equation for $0\\le x\\le2\\pi$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan x&=\\sqrt3\\\\x&=\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{4\\pi}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=\\frac{4\\pi}{3}$, $\\cos x=-\\frac12$, so $2\\cos x+1=0$. The numerator and denominator of the original expression are both $0$, so it is undefined and $x=\\frac{4\\pi}{3}$ is rejected.\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$: $\\frac{\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{3}+\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{3}}{\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{3}+\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{3}+1}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{1}=\\sqrt3$ ✓\nTherefore $x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
  },
